## Context

A web-based e-commerce application built with PHP and MySQL that focuses on authenticated storefront access, user account management, and structured order fulfillment between admins, couriers, and customers.

## Problem

Without structured authentication and dedicated administrative views, managing user accounts, password resets, stock updates, and delivery handoffs becomes error-prone as order volume grows.

## My role

Owner: I designed the relational data structure, implemented authentication and role-based dashboards in PHP, and deployed the containerized live demo on Render.

## As-is analysis

Reviewing standard storefront fulfillment highlighted the need for clear boundaries between customer-facing order tracking and internal admin/courier order operations, along with self-service account recovery.

## Requirements

- User authentication with login, logout, and forgot-password recovery (`login.php`, `forgot_password.php`).
- Role-specific dashboards for Admin and Courier operations alongside customer checkout and order history.
- Centralized user management and inventory management modules.
- Dedicated order detail views tailored to admin administration (`order-details-admin.php`) versus customer tracking (`order-details.php`).

## Solution design

The system routes authenticated sessions directly into role-appropriate interfaces (`admin_dashboard.php`, `courier_dashboard.php`, storefront checkout) backed by shared MySQL tables for users, products, and orders.

## Build

Implemented with PHP, MySQL, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and Docker, deployed at `ecommerce2-demo.onrender.com/login.php`. Core modules include authentication and recovery, `management-user.php`, `inventory_management.php`, `checkout.php`, `order-history.php`, `fetch_order_details.php`, and separate admin and customer order detail views. Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/E-Commerce2](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/E-Commerce2).

## Verification

Tested login flows, role-based dashboard routing, inventory management, and order detail views inside the Dockerized Render deployment.

## Outcome

Delivered an authenticated, multi-role PHP e-commerce web application available as an interactive live demo.

## Reflection

Separating admin order views from customer order views prevented accidental exposure of internal operational controls while keeping both sides easy to navigate.
